   "evidence": "VolumeForm.lean:18-19 (\"`\u03b5^{0123} = -1`, the convention of Peskin\u2013Schroeder\") and 43-44; CliffordAlgebraExtensions.lean:285-292 (`-4 * I) * (leviCivitaSymbol ![\u03bc, \u03bd, \u03c1, \u03c3]`, \"normalized by `\u03b5(0, 1, 2, 3) = 1`\", with the \u03b3's carrying upper indices); DIS/Tensors/Basic.lean:245-246. With `\u03b7 = (+,-,-,-)`, `\u03b5^{0123} = \u03b7^{00}\u03b7^{11}\u03b7^{22}\u03b7^{33}\u03b5_{0123} = -\u03b5_{0123}`, so the two normalisations differ by an overall sign.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/VolumeForm.lean",
   "fix": "Either define `volumeForm := -basisFin4.det` so that the contraction with four vectors realises `\u03b5^{0123} = +1` (P&S, and the normalisation implied by `trace_\u03b35_mul_\u03b3_mul_\u03b3_mul_\u03b3_mul_\u03b3`), or keep `\u03b5_{0123} = +1` and correct the documentation: drop the Peskin\u2013Schroeder attribution and state plainly that `volumeForm` is the negative of the `\u03b5^{0123} = +1` convention used by the \u03b3\u2085 trace identity, so that downstream T-odd/parity-odd instantiations insert the compensating sign.",
   "issue": "The docstring claims `\u03b5_{0123} = 1`, i.e. `\u03b5^{0123} = -1`, is \"the convention of Peskin\u2013Schroeder\" (repeated in the References, lines 43\u201344). Peskin\u2013Schroeder fix `\u03b5^{0123} = +1` (equivalently `\u03b5_{0123} = -1`), the opposite overall sign. The repo already encodes `\u03b5^{0123} = +1`: `trace_\u03b35_mul_\u03b3_mul_\u03b3_mul_\u03b3_mul_\u03b3` (CliffordAlgebraExtensions.lean:290) proves `tr(\u03b35\u03b3^\u03bc\u03b3^\u03bd\u03b3^\u03c1\u03b3^\u03c3) = -4i\u00b7\u03b5(\u03bc,\u03bd,\u03c1,\u03c3)` with `\u03b5(0,1,2,3) = 1`, which is the standard `tr[\u03b3^\u03bc\u03b3^\u03bd\u03b3^\u03c1\u03b3^\u03c3\u03b3^5] = -4i\u03b5^{\u03bc\u03bd\u03c1\u03c3}`. Since DIS/Tensors/Basic.lean:246 says the `\u03b5^{0123}` and `\u03b3\u2085` sign conventions \"sit in the choice of `\u03b5`\", supplying this `volumeForm` as that `\u03b5` yields a parity-odd structure with the wrong relative sign.",
   "line": 18
  }
 ],
